=== tk ===
tk 1.0.0
Minimal task tracker. Append-only JSON records in .tasks/ — no daemons, no
runtime.

Usage: tk [FLAGS] <SUBCOMMAND>

Commands:
  accept      Add or show acceptance criteria
  add         Create a task
  apply       Apply a batch of intents from stdin under one lock
  archive     Archive a done/closed task without deleting it
  block       Add a blocker dependency
  check       Check store integrity (non-zero exit on findings)
  checkpoint  Replace the current checkpoint (one summary, not the log)
              [aliases: ck]
  clean       Remove old completed tasks (archives by default)
  close       Close/cancel a task
  config      Show or set configuration
  defer       Defer a task
  done        Complete a task
  edit        Edit a task
  evidence    Add or show completion evidence
  init        Initialize .tasks/ in the current directory
  link        Add links to research, decisions, or source locations
  list        List tasks [aliases: ls]
  lock        Run a command while holding the store mutation lock
  log         Add a log entry to a task
  mv          Move a task to a different project
  open        Reset a task status to open
  path        Print the resolved task store location
  purge       Delete a task record [aliases: rm]
  ready       List active/open unblocked tasks [aliases: rdy]
  recover     Drop a record's torn last line (from an interrupted write)
  relate      Record a non-blocking relationship with another task
  show        Show task details
  start       Start working on a task (open → active) [aliases: active]
  unarchive   Return an archived task to active views
  unblock     Remove a blocker dependency
  unlink      Remove links from a task
  unrelate    Remove a non-blocking relationship
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Flags:
  -j, --json             Output as JSON
  -C, --dir <DIR>        Run in a different directory
      --tasks-dir <DIR>  Task store directory: exact path, must already exist
                         (no discovery)
  -h, --help             Print help
  -V, --version          Print version

=== tk init ===
Initialize .tasks/ in the current directory

Usage: tk init [-P --project <PROJECT>]

Flags:
  -P, --project <PROJECT>  Project name (default: directory name)
  -h, --help               Print help

Global flags:
  -j, --json               Output as JSON
  -C, --dir <DIR>          Run in a different directory
      --tasks-dir <DIR>    Task store directory: exact path, must already exist
                           (no discovery)

=== tk add ===
Create a task

Usage: tk add [FLAGS] <TITLE>…

Arguments:
  <TITLE>…  Task title

Flags:
  -p, --priority <PRIORITY>    Priority (0-4, p0-p4, or
                               none/urgent/high/medium/low)
  -P, --project <PROJECT>      Project (display grouping; identity is
                               unaffected)
  -d, --desc <DESC>            Description
  -l, --labels <LABELS>        Labels (comma-separated, repeatable)
  -A, --assignees <ASSIGNEES>  Assignees (comma-separated, repeatable)
      --parent <PARENT>        Parent task (alias, ID, or ID prefix)
      --estimate <ESTIMATE>    Estimate (user-defined units)
      --due <DUE>              Due date (YYYY-MM-DD or relative +Nh/+Nd/+Nw/+Nm)
  -h, --help                   Print help

Global flags:
  -j, --json                   Output as JSON
  -C, --dir <DIR>              Run in a different directory
      --tasks-dir <DIR>        Task store directory: exact path, must already
                               exist (no discovery)

=== tk list ===
List tasks

Usage: tk list [FLAGS] [SEARCH]…

Arguments:
  [SEARCH]…  Search title, description, alias, and ID

Flags:
  -a, --all                  Show all, including done and closed
      --archived             Show archived tasks only
  -s, --status <STATUS>      Filter by status (open/active/deferred/done/closed)
  -p, --priority <PRIORITY>  Filter by priority
  -P, --project <PROJECT>    Filter by project
  -l, --label <LABEL>        Filter by label
      --assignee <ASSIGNEE>  Filter by assignee
      --parent <PARENT>      Filter by parent task
      --roots                Top-level tasks only
      --overdue              Overdue tasks only
  -n, --limit <LIMIT>        Limit results
                             (default: 20)
  -h, --help                 Print help

Global flags:
  -j, --json                 Output as JSON
  -C, --dir <DIR>            Run in a different directory
      --tasks-dir <DIR>      Task store directory: exact path, must already
                             exist (no discovery)

