=== tk edit ===
Edit a task

Usage: tk edit [FLAGS] <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>  Task alias, ID, or ID prefix

Flags:
  -t, --title <TITLE>             New title
  -p, --priority <PRIORITY>       New priority
  -l, --labels <LABELS>           Labels: `+add` a value, or bare values to
                                  replace the set

                                  A leading `-` is read as a flag by the shell
                                  and this parser alike, so removal is
                                  `--remove-label`; `-l +x` and `--labels=-x`
                                  both work.
      --remove-label <REMOVE_LABEL>  Labels to remove (comma-separated)
  -A, --assignees <ASSIGNEES>     Assignees: `+add` a value, or bare values to
                                  replace the set
      --remove-assignee <REMOVE_ASSIGNEE>  Assignees to remove (comma-separated)
      --due <DUE>                 Due date (YYYY-MM-DD, relative, or - to clear)
      --parent <PARENT>           Parent task (or - to clear)
  -d, --desc <DESC>               Description (or - to clear)
      --estimate <ESTIMATE>       Estimate (or 0 to clear)
      --if-rev <REV>              Reject the edit unless the task still has this
                                  revision (`show --json`)
  -h, --help                      Print help

Global flags:
  -j, --json                      Output as JSON
  -C, --dir <DIR>                 Run in a different directory
      --tasks-dir <DIR>           Task store directory: exact path, must already
                                  exist (no discovery)

=== tk checkpoint ===
Replace the current checkpoint (one summary, not the log)

Usage: tk checkpoint [--clear] [--if-rev <REV>] <ID> [TEXT]…

Arguments:
  <ID>     Task alias, ID, or ID prefix
  [TEXT]…  Checkpoint text: current result, blocker, next action, verification

Flags:
      --clear            Clear the checkpoint
      --if-rev <REV>     Reject the update unless the task still has this
                         revision
  -h, --help             Print help

Global flags:
  -j, --json             Output as JSON
  -C, --dir <DIR>        Run in a different directory
      --tasks-dir <DIR>  Task store directory: exact path, must already exist
                         (no discovery)

=== tk link ===
Add links to relevant research, decisions, or source locations

A link is a document reference. Use `tk relate` for another task.

Usage: tk link <ID> [REFS]…

Arguments:
  <ID>     Task alias, ID, or ID prefix
  [REFS]…  References to add (paths, URLs); with none, list them

Flags:
  -h, --help             Print help

Global flags:
  -j, --json             Output as JSON
  -C, --dir <DIR>        Run in a different directory
      --tasks-dir <DIR>  Task store directory: exact path, must already exist
                         (no discovery)

